A||||12||btoth||West Coast Fiero Flowmaster?||||1||
Z||000000||btoth||06-24-2001||11:08 PM||||Does anyone have it installed and was it any trouble to <I>get</I> installed?<P>I had the 80 series muffler but NO shops in my area would even attempt the install even after long talks and pictures showing the final outcome.  So I returned it.  Of course, after returning it, my stock muffler now sound like absolute crap.  Is the West Coast flowmaster close enough to the original size that the shops would have any problem with it? (In other words... do they have to do any extra work?)<P>And how exactly has this muffler been modified to fit the Fiero?<P>Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||KRMFiero||06-25-2001||12:11 AM||||I am not positve but i think that they modified it to stock Fiero muffler size and stuff so it is a direct bolt in (well weld in/clamp in) e-mail them and ask||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bruce||06-25-2001||04:36 AM||||Contact Spintech mufflers via the web and give them the specs of your Fiero. They will give you the model number you need. Their mufflers seem to give better overall results and price as compared to Flowmaster. Also, campare delivery time from Spintech and West Coast Fiero, respectively.<BR>DXR-DAD can add a little here....||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||06-25-2001||10:47 AM||||Here's another post about mufflers?:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011242.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011242.html</A> <P>give Eric a call to make sure they have them in stock and the ETA! All and all I was happy with West Coast on this deal. I spoke to Eric on the land line and we exchanged a few emails before and after I bought the spin tech.<P>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000004||btoth||06-25-2001||11:25 AM||||OK, well I already knew that I loved the Flowmaster sound, which is why I had wanted one.  But I'm not that picky.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Right now my muffler sounds <I>bad</I>, but I don't want to replace it with a stock one.<P>Been doing some research.  Thanks DXR_DAD, I didn't see that thread.  It had a few bits of info that were useful.  I had read a bunch before my other muffler purchase and read some more before I started this thread but most of them didn't stay "on topic" for long.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I've spent all morning so far on the Spintech website and got this info:<P>Looking at their muffler diagrams, I found that their 311SC model is a 13x9x4 with 2" in and dual 2" out.  Which (if I have my stock muffler sizes of 12x9-5/8x5 right) means that it's only an inch longer than stock, which should be doable by <I>any</I> shop, correct??  In the thread that DXR_DAD linked to, I saw that terryk is/was using their 331SC model, which is the same thing but with a 2.5" in as opposed to the 2" in on the other one.<P>Would I be best off to go with the 2" in seeing as how I'm not planning on running bigger pipe?  How does the spintech sound compared to a flowmaster?  Is it rumbly.  I like rumbly mufflers.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks for the input!||||reg||1
Z||000005||WampusCat||06-25-2001||11:47 AM||||In a test in one of the 4X4 magazines, the Dynomax mufflers gave more performance than Flowmasters or anything else they tested.  They're made by the same co. that makes Walker mufflers and Monroe shocks and many parts stores carry them.  They don't list the Fiero on their website, but they make mufflers for Beretta/Corsica and Camaro/Firebird with 2.8.  Wonder if these could work?||||reg||1
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||06-25-2001||11:48 AM||||Im sure Eric (West Coast) will fill in the blanks for ya  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I know he will see this and give you some more info on the fit, sound and price. As stated in the other post, mine is not installed yet??? but yes it is about a inch longer. I will be doing the install myself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> so Im sure it will fit!! I'll get it in. I have a pic with it next to a stock muffler but I can't find it, I'll look again when I get home and post it here if I find it<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||06-25-2001||01:02 PM||||Delivery time should certainly be considered. Contact Spintech directly. They are on the web. I had mine in 3 days.||||reg||1
Z||000008||btoth||06-25-2001||07:59 PM||||I don't really care much about performance statistics, I just want something aftermarket that fits and sounds good.  (Kinda like a Flowmaster.)<P>Terryk, your's worked just fine?  Was it a straight forward install... no one around here wants to have to think no matter how much money you pay them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  <P>I'm prolly going to call Spintech tomorrow and just order the 311SC muffler, and pray that it will get installed.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||DXR_DAD||06-25-2001||11:09 PM||||Here's that pic!<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=13270947&p=50378527&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P>As you can see the case may be close to the same size? but it's the inlet and outlet pipes that will need some work. Still doesn't look like a hard job.<P><BR>DXR_DAD ||||reg||3
Z||000010||terryk||06-26-2001||12:17 AM||||I used the 331SC with 2.5" in and dual 2" out since I have the 3800SC in there. 2.5" pipes aren't fun to bend and fit.<P>The only change they made during the installation was they didn't used the muffler springs and used better hangers on the outlets to support it. It ain't coming out of there. <P>The shop that did mine didn't seem to be too upset although they commented about stuffing 2.5" pipe in there.<P>The 311SC which I believe is 2 or 2.25" in would be far easier to install.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 06-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Bruce||06-26-2001||05:17 PM||||I have the West Coast Flowmaster muffler installed on my 86 GT. There's no appreciable sound difference from the stock model, but it was a simple installation and a well built muffler.<BR>Walker (Dynomax) was the OEM supplier of mufflers for the Fiero. Last time I looked they were more expensive than either the Spintech or the Flowmaster.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Bruce||06-26-2001||08:52 PM||||Incidentally, Spintech recommends the 311SC ($115.95) for the Fiero.||||reg||1
